mca:evidence-adams-gallery-2008 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The earliest documents held in this collection: two messages sent within about twenty minutes of each other on the evening of 2008-08-08 to the Ansel Adams organisation, one carrying eight loose photographs of the print and one carrying the archive later sent to the auction house. They precede the museum letter by two days and the auction house by five, and they identify the body that letter miscalls the Ansel Adams Museum in San Francisco. The message carrying the archive retains its original Hotmail headers; the other has been rewritten by a later platform, and their relative order is not settled.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r9b0, _:b0_r9b1;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-consignment-photographs-2008, mca:evidence-sfmoma-approach-2008, mca:evidence-sothebys-approach-2008, _:b0_r9b10, _:b0_r9b11, _:b0_r9b12, _:b0_r9b2, _:b0_r9b3, _:b0_r9b4, _:b0_r9b5, _:b0_r9b6, _:b0_r9b7, _:b0_r9b8, _:b0_r9b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r9b13;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: the approach to the Ansel Adams organisation (8-9 August 2008)";
    la:member_of mca:collection.
mca:evidence-archived-websites-2013-2016 crm:P129_is_about mca:art-notes, mca:concept-metaconceptual-art, mca:wtfisart-reconstruction;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The Internet Archive holds dated captures of two domains the studio ran, and those captures are public and checkable by anyone. On www.wtfisart.com: a capture of 2013-07-20 showing only 'Under Construction:Check back soon !', and captures of 2014-12-18 and 2016-01-11 showing a site whose menu reads 'Artists', 'Art Market Reform is a happening' and 'Got Provenance ?', and whose text reads 'For the Love of God, We are the Art. Long Live the Art Spirit !', alongside the phrases 'Art is Capital invest with confidence' and 'What Hedge Funds ?! invest in Art'. On www.sunandrainworks.com: captures of 2016-01-26 and 2016-03-27 carrying the eight defining characteristics of Metaconceptual Art in full, in the same wording as the 2012 posting recorded elsewhere in this collection. What these captures establish is that the concept, its eight characteristics, and the studio's art-market vocabulary were published on the studio's own domains and preserved by a third party on dates no one in the studio controls. What they do not establish is anything about the auction of 2009: no capture mentions it, or lot 16, or Ansel Adams, or Sotheby's.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r10b0, _:b0_r10b1;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-pastebin-2011-2012, _:b0_r10b2, _:b0_r10b3, _:b0_r10b4, _:b0_r10b5, _:b0_r10b6, _:b0_r10b7, _:b0_r10b8, _:b0_r10b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r10b10;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: the studio's websites as captured by the Internet Archive (2013-2016)";
    la:member_of mca:collection.
mca:evidence-consignment-agreement-2009 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "The executed consignment agreement between Sotheby's, Inc. and the studio principal for the sale of 30 March 2009, together with the two emails that carried it. On 2009-03-18 the administrator of the Photographs department sent a scanned PDF of the agreement, writing that a signed agreement was required before the photograph could be sold. On 2009-03-19 the studio returned a signed PDF as an attachment named 'JoeArtChirum.pdf', with a covering note hoping the electronic format was suitable. That file is held. It runs to seven scanned pages: a six-page agreement on Sotheby's letterhead, dated 18-Mar-2009, addressed to the studio principal, naming Sotheby's principal auctioneer, carrying the consignor's signature above the line 'Consignor - Accepted and agreed' and a countersignature for Sotheby's, Inc.; and one further page of identity verification. This is the instrument of consignment itself, and the point at which the consignment ceases to be an inference from correspondence. Neither the document nor its terms are published here, for two independent reasons set out below.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r11b0, _:b0_r11b1;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-sothebys-approach-2008, _:b0_r11b10, _:b0_r11b11, _:b0_r11b2, _:b0_r11b3, _:b0_r11b4, _:b0_r11b5, _:b0_r11b6, _:b0_r11b7, _:b0_r11b8, _:b0_r11b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r11b12;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: the executed Sotheby's consignment agreement (March 2009)";
    la:member_of mca:collection.
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-photographs-2008#visual-item> a crm:E36_Visual_Item;
    rdfs:label "Verso credit block and inked annotations of the Ansel Adams print";
    la:digitally_shown_by <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/images/adams-verso-2008.jpg>, <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/images/adams-verso-full-2008.jpg>.
mca:evidence-consignment-photographs-2008 crm:P104_is_subject_to _:b0_r12b0;
    crm:P129_is_about mca:auction-as-artwork, mca:production-live-auction-2009, mca:sothebys-photographs-auction-2009, mca:wtf-is-ansel-adams;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-consignment-photographs-2008#visual-item>;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "Sun & Rain Works holds eleven digital photographs, taken in a single session on 2008-08-08, that document a matted black-and-white photographic print in the studio's possession. The sequence records the print recto, the mount, the verso with its backing and hanging wire, and a close-up of the verso credit block. In one frame the print is photographed together with a copy of Andy Warhol's 'The Philosophy of Andy Warhol (From A to B and Back Again)', placed upright and facing the camera. The close-up of the verso shows a printed credit block reading 'Photograph by Ansel Adams for The American Trust Company', a negative number beginning '1-SF-', the beginning of a handwritten title 'San Francisco fr...', and a hand-inked annotation 'Wells Fargo Bank' written over the struck-through word 'THE'. These markings correspond, in four independent particulars, to the markings recorded in the public Sotheby's catalogue entry for lot 16 of Photographs, sale N08533 (2009) - the Ansel Adams print 'San Francisco from Twin Peaks'. The photographs therefore evidence that a print bearing the markings described in the lot-16 catalogue entry was in the studio's possession nearly eight months before that sale of 30 March 2009, and that it was documented there alongside an art-referential object. They do not establish the identity of the consignor of record, and they establish no precedence over any later artist, work, or event.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r12b1, _:b0_r12b2;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863, aat:300215302;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-sothebys-approach-2008, _:b0_r12b10, _:b0_r12b3, _:b0_r12b4, _:b0_r12b5, _:b0_r12b6, _:b0_r12b7, _:b0_r12b8, _:b0_r12b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r12b11;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: documentation photographs of the Ansel Adams print (August 2008)";
    la:member_of mca:collection.
mca:evidence-hosting-receipts-2009 crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "A domain registrar's billing record for the studio's account, held as the registrar's own comma-separated export for 2009 together with forty-two PDF invoices, running from 2009-01-04 to 2016-01-05. It shows that on 2009-03-16 at 00:45:06 UTC the account registered the domain WTFISART.COM, on receipt 158832568, for $1.99 plus a $0.20 ICANN fee; that at 01:07:15 UTC the same night it bought 'Economy Classic Hosting Linux' for wtfisart.com at $4.99, on receipt 158833357; and that the hosting was then paid for monthly, at $4.99 with a zero-rated bandwidth line, on 2009-04-15, 2009-05-15, 2009-06-15, 2009-07-25, 2009-08-15, 2009-09-15, 2009-10-15, 2009-11-15 and 2009-12-15. In the same transaction as the domain registration the account also bought an 'Economy Quick Blogcast' for $9.98, which was refunded at 01:20:25 UTC that night on receipt 158832568R, thirty-five minutes after purchase. Separately the account registered GROWINGALOHA.COM on 2009-01-04 and renewed it on 2010-01-05. This is a third party's business record of the studio's account, and it dates the domain and its hosting from fourteen days before the Sotheby's sale of 30 March 2009. The invoices continue past that first year under a second account number, and the paragraphs below set out what they add: the re-registration of WTFISART.COM in 2011, the registration of METACONCEPTUALART.COM in the same order, and renewals running to 2016.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r13b0, _:b0_r13b1;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-archived-websites-2013-2016, mca:evidence-wtfia-2009, _:b0_r13b10, _:b0_r13b11, _:b0_r13b2, _:b0_r13b3, _:b0_r13b4, _:b0_r13b5, _:b0_r13b6, _:b0_r13b7, _:b0_r13b8, _:b0_r13b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r13b12;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: the registrar's receipts for the studio's domains (2009-2016)";
    la:member_of mca:collection.
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-inscription-photograph-2011#visual-item-digital-work> a crm:E36_Visual_Item;
    rdfs:label "ArtHistoriansOTheFuture: the board's inscription as a digital work";
    la:digitally_shown_by <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/images/art-historians-of-the-future-2013.jpg>.
<https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-inscription-photograph-2011#visual-item> a crm:E36_Visual_Item;
    rdfs:label "Two studio works photographed together, the upper board inscribed about the art historians of the future and the sheet beneath it inscribed 'W.T.F. is Art ?'";
    la:digitally_shown_by <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/images/wtf-is-art-sheet-2011.jpg>.
mca:evidence-inscription-photograph-2011 crm:P129_is_about mca:art-notes, mca:wtfisart;
    crm:P138i_has_representation <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-inscription-photograph-2011#visual-item-digital-work>, <https://www.metaconceptualart.com/data/linked-art/evidence-inscription-photograph-2011#visual-item>;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "One digital photograph, held by the studio, taken with a camera phone and recording its capture as 2011-11-08 12:18:15. It shows two works laid one on the other. On top is a narrow board inscribed by hand in purple marker: '\"Helping the Art Historians of the future to keep their Employment\" (Here and Now. ~)'. Beneath it is a large sheet covered in small handwritten notes running at many angles, with a coloured spiral and strokes of coloured pencil; along its right-hand edge, written in quotation marks, it reads '\"W.T.F. is Art ?\"'. The studio identifies the board as the work 'Helping the Art Historians of the future' and the sheet as 'Dancing with Mummies', a title it gives as a reference to Thomas Hoving, the former director of the Metropolitan Museum of Art, and to what it calls its archaeology of the art world. Neither physical work survives, by the studio's account, and this photograph is the only known record of the sheet. The board was the foundation of a digital work, ArtHistoriansOTheFuture, which the studio posted publicly to Flickr on 2013-06-02. The photograph dates the phrase W.T.F. is Art, written on a physical work, to November 2011 at the latest, and the board's phrase to nineteen months before that posting and twenty-two months before the studio used the same words in its letter of 2013-09-12 to a university art museum.";
    crm:P1_is_identified_by _:b0_r14b0, _:b0_r14b1;
    crm:P2_has_type aat:300026906, aat:300055863, aat:300215302;
    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by mca:evidence-archived-websites-2013-2016, mca:evidence-hosting-receipts-2009, mca:evidence-museum-correspondence-2013, _:b0_r14b10, _:b0_r14b2, _:b0_r14b3, _:b0_r14b4, _:b0_r14b5, _:b0_r14b6, _:b0_r14b7, _:b0_r14b8, _:b0_r14b9;
    crm:P94i_was_created_by _:b0_r14b11;
    a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object;
    rdfs:label "Evidence archive: a photograph of two studio works inscribed 'W.T.F. is Art ?' (8 November 2011)";
